  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Integrated Multi-sectoral Assistance to Vulnerable Displaced Population in Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the collapse of the Somali central government in 1991, Somalia has suffered an overly complex protracted conflict characterized by changing political dynamics and power shifts. In 2024, Somalia is expected to continue to face a precarious situation as it still grapples with a convergence of complex challenges, including the ongoing impacts of climate change, security instability, and humanitarian crises. To address the acute needs of displaced and vulnerable Somalis, the International Organization for Migration is proposing a comprehensive and integrated water, sanitation and hygiene and shelter and non-food items intervention, with the overall coordination and support from camp coordination and camp management teams, with the main objective to ensure dignified, safe and secure living conditions and basic services for vulnerable populations affected disasters driven by natural hazards and conflict.</narrative>
  </description>
